{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_readme": "Proposed calibration for JeremyABurton/1st-downs, the shadow evidence campaign's first consumer (D-135). Authored for that repository from the read-only field study of 2026-09-03, in which all 45 of its pull requests were measurable; its owners edit it before it lands, and nothing here is copied from another repository's calibration. Every rule is proposed, as D-064 requires, so this policy can only ever describe what a route would have been; a proposed rule never runs less than everything.",
  "classifier": {
    "surfaces": [
      {
        "glob": "**/*.md",
        "surface": "docs",
        "effect": "prose",
        "breadth": "leaf"
      },
      {
        "_note": "SKILL.md is instruction, not description. A change here can alter what every agent does, so it is never only documentation.",
        "glob": "**/SKILL.md",
        "surface": "skill-policy",
        "effect": "public-contract",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "glob": "**/scripts/*.py",
        "surface": "product",
        "effect": "behavior",
        "breadth": "runtime"
      },
      {
        "_note": "Tests are verification authority. Weakening one changes what the repository can claim, which is why this cannot be a cheap route.",
        "glob": "**/tests/*.py",
        "surface": "tests",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "glob": "**/assets/*.json",
        "surface": "schema",
        "effect": "public-contract",
        "breadth": "cross-runtime"
      },
      {
        "_note": "A workflow decides which checks run at all. Same reasoning as tests, one level up.",
        "glob": ".github/workflows/**",
        "surface": "ci",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository",
        "sensitivity": "release"
      },
      {
        "_note": "The router and the receipt writer decide what every other change is allowed to skip. Left as ordinary product code they graded themselves: with the rules below approved, a change to the router took the Level 2 product route. Entries below this line exist because a classifier is what makes a path authority, and load_policy refuses a policy that omits them. See D-071. This entry names the shipped skill's own scripts in the source spelling and the next names every installed spelling; the earlier **/scripts/*.py reached every nested scripts directory of an installing repository. See D-107 and D-118.",
        "glob": "anti-dark-code/scripts/*.py",
        "surface": "product",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "glob": "**/anti-dark-code/scripts/*.py",
        "surface": "product",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "glob": "**/scripts/adc_receipt.py",
        "surface": "product",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "_note": "The installer and distribution controls decide which skill a repository is running at all.",
        "glob": "**/scripts/adc.py",
        "surface": "product",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "_note": "The capability catalog defines what verification means. A change here can retire an obligation without touching a test.",
        "glob": "**/assets/verification-capabilities.json",
        "surface": "schema",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "_note": "Installed and shipped calibration: the routing policy itself, the gate configuration, and the verification plan. A policy that could route its own edits cheaply could approve its own shortcut.",
        "glob": "**/calibration/*.json",
        "surface": "schema",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
      {
        "glob": "anti-dark-code/SOURCE-SCOPE.json",
        "surface": "schema",
        "effect": "verification-authority",
        "breadth": "repository"
      },
